To create an input field with a clickable SVG icon (a reading glass icon) on the right side, you can use HTML and CSS to style it. Below is an example of how to achieve this functionality. The SVG icon will be clickable, and you can define an `onClick` function that will be called when the icon is pressed.

Here's a basic example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Input with SVG Icon</title>
    <style>
        .input-container {
            position: relative;
            width: 300px; /* Set the width you want */
        }
        .input-field {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px 40px 10px 10px; /* Add padding to make space for the icon */
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }
        .icon {
            position: absolute;
            right: 10px;
            top: 50%;
            transform: translateY(-50%);
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="input-container">
    <input type="text" class="input-field" id="searchInput" placeholder="Type something...">
    <svg class="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" onclick="handleClick()">
        <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10 18a8 8 0 1 0 0-16 8 8 0 0 0 0 16zm8 0l6 6m-6-6l-6-6" />
    </svg>
</div>

<script>
    function handleClick() {
        const input = document.getElementById('searchInput').value;
        console.log('Input value:', input);
        // Add your desired functionality here
    }
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **HTML Structure**: We have a `div` container class `input-container` that contains the input field and the SVG icon.
- **CSS Styles**: 
  - The `.input-container` is positioned relatively to contain its absolutely positioned children.
  - The input field (`.input-field`) has padding to prevent text from overlapping with the SVG icon.
  - The SVG icon is positioned absolutely within the container, aligned to the right.
- **SVG Icon**: The reading glass icon's path is defined in the `d` attribute. You can customize it or replace it with another SVG if you prefer.
- **JavaScript**: The `handleClick` function retrieves the value of the input when the icon is clicked and logs it. You can replace the `console.log` with whatever functionality you want to implement.

### Customization:
Feel free to adjust the styling to suit your UI requirements and replace the SVG with any other icon as needed!

